<title>UK: Britain's National Grid to sue Pakistan.</title>
<headline>Britain's National Grid to sue Pakistan.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's National Grid said on Wednesday that it is suing the Pakistan government for $21 million for the cancellation of the Jamshoro-Lahore overhead power lines project.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the compensation sum includes the expenses of the project developers and contractors.  </p>
<p>National Grid, which owns and operates the national electricity transmission grid in England and Wales, said its share of expenses for the project for 1996/97 was around $2.4 million.</p>
<p>&quot;National Grid regrets having to take this action, but still hopes that an amicable resolution can be reached,&quot; said Peter Gavan, director of corporate affairs.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
